course: dictionary
lesson: 7653
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is meant by reading the context, the words and sentences around it. «Promote» is a good example. It can mean to move someone up to a higher job, to help something grow, or to advertise something.
explain: Look at «She was promoted to manager.» The clue is the job: a manager has a higher job, so promoted means moved up. Now read «Exercise promotes good health.» There is no job here at all. Exercise helps good health grow, so promotes means helps.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about: a job, health, a film, a shop or a football team. Each one points to a different meaning. «Stars go on chat shows mainly to promote a new film, book or tour» is about advertising, because the star wants people to go and see or buy it.
explain: Then test your meaning. Swap it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Promote has several meanings, so the context tells you which one to use.
fact: «Promote» can mean to move someone to a higher job or rank.
fact: «Promote» can mean to help something grow or happen, as in «Exercise promotes good health.»
fact: «Promote» can mean to advertise something so that people want to buy it or come to it.
fact: In UK and Irish football, a team that is promoted moves up to a higher league.
exercise: «She was promoted to manager.» What does promoted mean here? | Moved to a smaller office | Sent home early | *Moved up to a higher job | Given a new hat
exercise: «Exercise promotes good health.» What does promotes mean here? | Stops people from getting ill | Shouts about health | *Helps good health grow | Makes things cheaper
exercise: «Our shop will promote the new trainers with big posters.» What does promote mean here? | Take the trainers back | Help a plant grow | *Advertise, to make people want to buy them | Move someone to a higher rank
test: «Stars go on chat shows mainly to promote a new film.» Which meaning is used? | Give the film a higher job | Help the film grow bigger | Make the film shorter | *Advertise the film to make people go and see it
test: «The football team was promoted after winning the league.» What does it mean? | Given a new kit | Sent home from the match | Moved down to a lower league | *Moved up to a higher league
exam: «An endorsement is when a famous person promotes a product; it does not prove they really use it.» What does promotes mean here? | Stops people from buying it | Helps the product grow bigger | *Advertises the product to make people want it | Moves the product to a higher shelf
